(a) Capture filters (typed in Capture > Options) 

host 192.168.1.10                   # all traffic to/from this host 
net 192.168.1.0/24                  # entire subnet 
src host 192.168.1.10               # only packets FROM this host 
dst port 53                         # traffic going TO port 53 (DNS) 
tcp port 443                        # only HTTPS/TLS traffic 
udp                                 # only UDP packets 
not arp and not broadcast           # ignore ARP and broadcasts 
tcp port 80 and host 192.168.1.10   # combined condition 

(b) Display filters (typed in the green filter bar) 

ip.addr == 192.168.1.10                      # any packet with this IP (src or dst) 
ip.src == 192.168.1.10                       # only where this IP is the source 
tcp.port == 80                               # HTTP over TCP 
http                                         # only HTTP protocol packets 
dns                                          # only DNS packets 
http.request.method == "GET"                 # only HTTP GET requests 
tcp.flags.syn == 1 && tcp.flags.ack == 0     # TCP connection starts (SYN) 
tcp.analysis.retransmission                  # retransmitted TCP segments 
ip.addr == 192.168.1.10 && tcp.port == 443   # host AND port together 
frame contains "password"                    # packets whose bytes contain the text
